WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:03.335
AGNES VAN RHIJN:<i> New York
 is a collection of villages.</i>

00:00:03.769 --> 00:00:06.206
<i> The old have been in charge
 since before the revolution...</i>

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:08.641
<i> until the new people invaded.</i>

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:11.811
♪ (DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYS) ♪

00:00:12.879 --> 00:00:14.814
MARIAN BROOK:<i> Well, I'm new.
 I've only just arrived.</i>

00:00:15.114 --> 00:00:17.550
You are my niece
and you belong to old New York.

00:00:20.253 --> 00:00:22.021
OSCAR VAN RHIJN:<i> George Russell
 is a power in the land.</i>

00:00:22.122 --> 00:00:23.656
Before long, he'll put money
into his pocket

00:00:23.756 --> 00:00:24.957
with every train ticket you buy.

00:00:25.057 --> 00:00:26.259
I think we should know
the Russell family.

00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:27.860
We do not move
in the same circles.

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:29.362
Momma, you are incorrigible.

00:00:29.462 --> 00:00:31.363
I take that
as the highest praise.

00:00:31.464 --> 00:00:32.998
Well, how do you
find your aunts?

00:00:33.098 --> 00:00:34.701
MARIAN:<i> Ada is kind,
 but not clever.</i>

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:37.370
And Agnes is clever,
but not kind.

00:00:38.838 --> 00:00:41.541
Mrs. Van Rhijn
and her sad sister
were spying on me today.

00:00:41.641 --> 00:00:43.242
I don't know why
you bother with them.

00:00:43.776 --> 00:00:45.144
BERTHA RUSSELL:
<i> I don't bother with them.</i>

00:00:45.244 --> 00:00:47.580
I'm afraid New York can be
quite challenging at first.

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:49.215
We haven't found it so,
have we George?

00:00:49.648 --> 00:00:52.318
There is no challenge
you are not equal to, my dear.

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:54.854
AGNES:<i> We have invited Marian
 to live with us.</i>

00:00:54.954 --> 00:00:55.955
<i> She hasn't a penny.</i>

00:00:56.389 --> 00:00:59.024
I cannot live
within Aunt Agnes' confines.

00:00:59.558 --> 00:01:02.695
AGNES:<i> You must meet the
 right people in the right way.</i>

00:01:04.063 --> 00:01:05.431
Money isn't everything, Agnes.

00:01:05.531 --> 00:01:06.231
(AGNES LAUGHS)

00:01:06.665 --> 00:01:08.468
I don't understand
why they have taken you in.

00:01:08.568 --> 00:01:10.703
PEGGY SCOTT:<i> I have a job
and the fresh start that I need.</i>

00:01:11.203 --> 00:01:12.538
I want to do something
with my life.

00:01:12.638 --> 00:01:15.508
For a New Yorker,
anything is possible.

00:01:16.309 --> 00:01:17.843
You are the future,
Mrs. Russell.

00:01:18.477 --> 00:01:20.713
<i> And if you are the future,
 then they must be the past.</i>

00:01:21.046 --> 00:01:23.316
Well, things move faster
nowadays.

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:26.151
I hope you're not
against Miss Scott.

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:27.386
SPEAKER:<i> She'll disrupt things.</i>

00:01:27.653 --> 00:01:29.622
Maybe we need
a bit of disruption.

00:01:29.722 --> 00:01:30.824
Let the tournament begin.

00:01:31.691 --> 00:01:32.357
♪ (MUSIC CONTINUES) ♪

00:01:32.891 --> 00:01:34.226
Why don't we just go outside
and roll in the gutter?

00:01:34.326 --> 00:01:35.628
<i> It will save time.</i>

00:01:37.396 --> 00:01:39.398
Do you know of Newport well,
Miss Russell?

00:01:39.832 --> 00:01:42.101
The mistress is not a player
in the great game.

00:01:42.702 --> 00:01:44.871
That woman is unsuitable
as an acquaintance.

00:01:46.405 --> 00:01:47.706
I'll make them pay one day.

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:49.843
SPEAKER 2:<i> How can anyone
 be so wretched?</i>

00:01:51.544 --> 00:01:53.446
You bastard.

00:01:53.546 --> 00:01:55.781
I may be a bastard,
Mr. Thorburn...

00:01:56.215 --> 00:01:57.116
but you are a fool.

00:01:57.683 --> 00:01:59.752
And of the two,
I think I know which I prefer.

